#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0288 expect=skipped domain=TS
#note "THE TSVAL ALL-FACET GATE (Fix #331 bucket 2, M2-D24 / M3-D18; pin owed by review S9, authored by Fix #340). The TS dataset declares no TSVAL column, so Requirements.Variables.All [TSVAL] rejects it and the rule is SKIPPED naming TSVAL. \u26a0 RE-NOTED at the R-5.25 split (2026-09-07): this note used to describe a bare empty(TSVAL) flooding on the absent column, and that mechanism moved. This half now reads `not empty(TSVAL) and not empty(TSVALNF)`, which is FALSE on an absent column and cannot flood -- the gate here only turns a silent zero into an auditable SKIP (R-4.11). The load-bearing copy of this pin is now on the sibling, CDISC-SEND-0288-A-skipped_no_tsval_column-TS, whose `empty(TSVAL) and empty(TSVALNF)` genuinely would fire on every row."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset TS class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSPARM   type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter"
col TSVALNF  type=Char label="Parameter Value Null Flavor"
---
S1 | TS | 1 | STSTDTC | Study Start Date |
S1 | TS | 2 | SPECIES | Species | NA
---
